+## Pre-register smart readers
+
+When placing a hardware order, you can pre-register eligible smart readers by selecting a Terminal location. When serial numbers become available, Stripe automatically registers each eligible smart reader to the selected location. You don’t need to register the readers manually after placing the order.
+
+If your account has access to the [Terminal Hardware Orders API](https://docs.stripe.com/terminal/fleet/order-and-return-readers.md#use-the-hardware-orders-api) preview, Stripe can emit device-level outcome events after automatic registration attempts: `terminal.hardware_order_device.registered` when a device is successfully registered to the selected location, or `terminal.hardware_order_device.registration_failed` when Stripe reports that a device failed to be registered. Each event’s `data.object` is the relevant [Terminal hardware order device](https://docs.stripe.com/api/terminal/hardware_order_devices/object.md), so you can correlate the result using its device ID, serial number, and hardware order relationship.
+
+You can change the selected Terminal location on the hardware order details page until serial numbers become available.
+
+You can pre-register each order to only one location. To register readers from the same order to multiple locations, wait until serial numbers become available, then register each reader individually by serial number.
 
